```js
const text = "july 7 1994 (age 7) London, UK (1994-07-07)";

// removes "(age 7)" where the number can be anything (and allows extra spaces)
const cleaned = text.replace(/\s*\(age\s*\d+\)\s*/i, " ").trim();

console.log(cleaned);
// -> "july 7 1994 London, UK (1994-07-07)"
```

If you want to remove **only** the `(age N)` part and keep spacing exactly, use:
```js
const cleaned2 = text.replace(/\(age\s*\d+\)/i, "").replace(/\s{2,}/g, " ").trim();
console.log(cleaned2);
```

